{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; source .venv/bin/activate; python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('planning.md')\np.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\n\n## Motivation & Novelty Assessment\n### Why This Research Matters\nReliable editing must distinguish intended semantic consequences from accidental damage. A computed arithmetic fact shares machinery with other computations, so locality on entity facts is not sufficient evidence for arithmetic isolation. Editing and unlearning practitioners benefit from an explicit scope-dependent frontier.\n### Gap in Existing Work\nThe gathered review motivates a computed-fact case study; it does not establish an exhaustive absence of prior work. Arithmetic mechanism papers motivate operand/output controls, but this study does not claim to identify helices or causal neurons.\n### Our Novel Contribution\nMeasure held-out arithmetic and factual leakage across restricted weight editing, preservation strength, training breadth and routing, with several independent edits/seeds and explicit local rewrite semantics.\n### Experiment Justification\n1. Restricted fine-tuning and KL strengths reveal efficacy versus collateral drift.\n2. Exact/canonical routing supplies a transparent architectural isolation control.\n3. Exact versus paraphrase training tests breadth at equal answer-token supervision; prompt-token totals will be recorded, so this is not called a fully token-matched SDF replication.\n\n## Frozen execution protocol (2026-10-04, before model experiments)\n**Models/resources.** RTX A6000 48 GiB; existing isolated .venv. Archive live OpenRouter catalog before selection. Use Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct locally because weight access, repeated restoration and affordable multi-seed editing are required; this is a resource-constrained controlled case study, not a contemporary frontier capability comparison. Pin HF revision. A catalog-verified current efficient API model supplies only an auxiliary prompt control, never a surrogate for training.\n**Independent variables.** Edit identity (2+2→5 primary; 2+2→6, 3+3→7, France capital→Rome robustness); optimization seeds 11/22/33; restricted single-layer FT, FT+KL (strengths 1/10), paraphrase FT+KL10, LoRA+KL10. Primary all five methods, secondary exact FT and FT+KL10. Add true-answer sham and routing controls.\n**Optimization.** Pilot dev-only learning rate: FT 2e-5, LoRA 1e-3; 40-step maximum, evaluate efficacy and dev drift at steps 0/5/10/20/40. Single middle/late MLP down projection (layer18/28); no claim of prior causal localization. Select earliest checkpoint with >=.95 exact target first-token probability and greedy correct target; otherwise maximal target probability. Replay16 sampled independently per step from 400 train sums and 128 train factual prompts. Four edit examples per step; supervised answer plus end-of-turn; breadth samples exact plus four train paraphrases. Stochasticity is replay/LoRA initialization. Equal update and supervised-token budgets; total input token discrepancy explicitly reported. ROME/MEMIT excluded because subject/covariance assumptions are unvalidated here.\n**Data/splits.** Primary all1879 held-out arithmetic rows, 128 CounterFact test prompts, 32 GSM8K test problems (exploratory capability only), 16 WikiText test passages capped64 tokens. CounterFact train supplies preservation prompts. Target train overlap is intentional; all other overlaps must be audited. Secondary edits use a deterministic transformed suite with recomputed local-rule oracle and remove their target from preservation. Selection uses dev only. Exact target, spacing, leading answer tokens and raw/chat formatting are checked first.\n**Metrics.** Greedy answer match and exact output agreement; arithmetic normalization only for unambiguous scalar answers. First-token target probability is a confidence diagnostic, not full response probability. Full-vocabulary KL on fixed reference prefixes and WikiText next-token NLL; same-prefix distributions only. Separate paraphrase, dependent, neighboring, distant, other-operation, factual and text strata. Report base-known accuracy denominators and all failures. No assertion of universal preservation or genuine belief.\n**Hypotheses/statistics.** H1: preservation reduces collateral drift at adequate efficacy. H2: broader training increases semantic transfer (possibly damage). H3: exact routing achieves literal isolation but little transfer. Primary contrasts KL10 versus FT and breadth versus KL10, paired across3 seeds; report seed range/SD and paired percentage-point effects. Exact sign-flip tests (8 permutations) cannot yield strong significance with3 seeds; report this instead of pseudoreplication. Descriptive family-cluster bootstrap95% intervals within the finite suite; distinguish these from population/model uncertainty. Holm correction for two primary contrasts. No powered universal null test; near-zero leakage is a finite-suite finding.\n**Expected outcomes and success criteria.** A useful result maps tradeoffs even when edits fail. Successful execution requires baseline audit, real weight updates, held-out raw outputs, multiple seeds/targets, explicit failed conditions, reproducible scripts/plots/report. Evidence for shallow isolation is high exact efficacy with low held-out transfer; evidence for depth requires dependency use and robustness, not only paraphrases.\n**Milestones.** Motivation/planning; setup/data+pilot; implementation+validation; all experiments; analysis; documentation+reproduction. Allow25% debugging buffer. Anticipated one-GPU runtime tens of minutes to a few hours, measured rather than promised. Store configs/logs/checkpoints incrementally. SDF-scale replication and mechanistic intervention are explicitly deferred within existing direction ranking.\n''')\ns=Path('STATE.md');t=s.read_text();a=t.index('<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:experiment_runner -->'\"');b=t.index('<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:experiment_runner -->'\"');s.write_text(t[:a]+'''<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:experiment_runner -->\nPhase0 motivation and Phase1 planning complete: reviewed resource handoff, upstream answer-masking trainer, dataset semantics and top3 fixed directions. Added motivation and frozen protocol to planning.md. Hardware A6000 49140MiB, existing .venv activated; dependency installation in progress. Live catalog saved results/openrouter_catalog.json. Local historical Qwen1.5B is justified for repeated weight-access experiments; not frontier ranking. Next Phase2: pin/download model, validate base formatting, build harness. No experimental outcomes yet. Breadth comparison matches supervised tokens/updates, not total input tokens; SDF replication deferred.\n'\"''' +t[b:])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; source .venv/bin/activate; python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('planning.md')\np.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\n\n## Motivation & Novelty Assessment\n### Why This Research Matters\nReliable editing must distinguish intended semantic consequences from accidental damage. A computed arithmetic fact shares machinery with other computations, so locality on entity facts is not sufficient evidence for arithmetic isolation. Editing and unlearning practitioners benefit from an explicit scope-dependent frontier.\n### Gap in Existing Work\nThe gathered review motivates a computed-fact case study; it does not establish an exhaustive absence of prior work. Arithmetic mechanism papers motivate operand/output controls, but this study does not claim to identify helices or causal neurons.\n### Our Novel Contribution\nMeasure held-out arithmetic and factual leakage across restricted weight editing, preservation strength, training breadth and routing, with several independent edits/seeds and explicit local rewrite semantics.\n### Experiment Justification\n1. Restricted fine-tuning and KL strengths reveal efficacy versus collateral drift.\n2. Exact/canonical routing supplies a transparent architectural isolation control.\n3. Exact versus paraphrase training tests breadth at equal answer-token supervision; prompt-token totals will be recorded, so this is not called a fully token-matched SDF replication.\n\n## Frozen execution protocol (2026-10-04, before model experiments)\n**Models/resources.** RTX A6000 48 GiB; existing isolated .venv. Archive live OpenRouter catalog before selection. Use Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct locally because weight access, repeated restoration and affordable multi-seed editing are required; this is a resource-constrained controlled case study, not a contemporary frontier capability comparison. Pin HF revision. A catalog-verified current efficient API model supplies only an auxiliary prompt control, never a surrogate for training.\n**Independent variables.** Edit identity (2+2→5 primary; 2+2→6, 3+3→7, France capital→Rome robustness); optimization seeds 11/22/33; restricted single-layer FT, FT+KL (strengths 1/10), paraphrase FT+KL10, LoRA+KL10. Primary all five methods, secondary exact FT and FT+KL10. Add true-answer sham and routing controls.\n**Optimization.** Pilot dev-only learning rate: FT 2e-5, LoRA 1e-3; 40-step maximum, evaluate efficacy and dev drift at steps 0/5/10/20/40. Single middle/late MLP down projection (layer18/28); no claim of prior causal localization. Select earliest checkpoint with >=.95 exact target first-token probability and greedy correct target; otherwise maximal target probability. Replay16 sampled independently per step from 400 train sums and 128 train factual prompts. Four edit examples per step; supervised answer plus end-of-turn; breadth samples exact plus four train paraphrases. Stochasticity is replay/LoRA initialization. Equal update and supervised-token budgets; total input token discrepancy explicitly reported. ROME/MEMIT excluded because subject/covariance assumptions are unvalidated here.\n**Data/splits.** Primary all1879 held-out arithmetic rows, 128 CounterFact test prompts, 32 GSM8K test problems (exploratory capability only), 16 WikiText test passages capped64 tokens. CounterFact train supplies preservation prompts. Target train overlap is intentional; all other overlaps must be audited. Secondary edits use a deterministic transformed suite with recomputed local-rule oracle and remove their target from preservation. Selection uses dev only. Exact target, spacing, leading answer tokens and raw/chat formatting are checked first.\n**Metrics.** Greedy answer match and exact output agreement; arithmetic normalization only for unambiguous scalar answers. First-token target probability is a confidence diagnostic, not full response probability. Full-vocabulary KL on fixed reference prefixes and WikiText next-token NLL; same-prefix distributions only. Separate paraphrase, dependent, neighboring, distant, other-operation, factual and text strata. Report base-known accuracy denominators and all failures. No assertion of universal preservation or genuine belief.\n**Hypotheses/statistics.** H1: preservation reduces collateral drift at adequate efficacy. H2: broader training increases semantic transfer (possibly damage). H3: exact routing achieves literal isolation but little transfer. Primary contrasts KL10 versus FT and breadth versus KL10, paired across3 seeds; report seed range/SD and paired percentage-point effects. Exact sign-flip tests (8 permutations) cannot yield strong significance with3 seeds; report this instead of pseudoreplication. Descriptive family-cluster bootstrap95% intervals within the finite suite; distinguish these from population/model uncertainty. Holm correction for two primary contrasts. No powered universal null test; near-zero leakage is a finite-suite finding.\n**Expected outcomes and success criteria.** A useful result maps tradeoffs even when edits fail. Successful execution requires baseline audit, real weight updates, held-out raw outputs, multiple seeds/targets, explicit failed conditions, reproducible scripts/plots/report. Evidence for shallow isolation is high exact efficacy with low held-out transfer; evidence for depth requires dependency use and robustness, not only paraphrases.\n**Milestones.** Motivation/planning; setup/data+pilot; implementation+validation; all experiments; analysis; documentation+reproduction. Allow25% debugging buffer. Anticipated one-GPU runtime tens of minutes to a few hours, measured rather than promised. Store configs/logs/checkpoints incrementally. SDF-scale replication and mechanistic intervention are explicitly deferred within existing direction ranking.\n''')\ns=Path('STATE.md');t=s.read_text();a=t.index('<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:experiment_runner -->'\"');b=t.index('<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:experiment_runner -->'\"');s.write_text(t[:a]+'''<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:experiment_runner -->\nPhase0 motivation and Phase1 planning complete: reviewed resource handoff, upstream answer-masking trainer, dataset semantics and top3 fixed directions. Added motivation and frozen protocol to planning.md. Hardware A6000 49140MiB, existing .venv activated; dependency installation in progress. Live catalog saved results/openrouter_catalog.json. Local historical Qwen1.5B is justified for repeated weight-access experiments; not frontier ranking. Next Phase2: pin/download model, validate base formatting, build harness. No experimental outcomes yet. Breadth comparison matches supervised tokens/updates, not total input tokens; SDF replication deferred.\n'\"''' +t[b:])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-2d1a-codex-gpt-6-astra\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
