{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"The sham run shows why “answer changed” cannot always be read as “knowledge damaged.” Some differences are harmless equation echoes or wording changes, while others are wrong arithmetic—for example, `0+9=` changing from `9` to `10`. I’m retaining the predeclared strict scores and adding a clearly labeled scoring sensitivity check for obvious formatting differences."}}
