{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; source .venv/bin/activate; python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('resources.md');p.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\n\n## Completed experiment execution (2026-10-04)\n\nThe experiment runner used the gathered arithmetic suite, CounterFact, WikiText-2 and GSM8K, and inspected the standard-FT answer-masking trainer. A fresh implementation in \"'`src/` avoids installing incompatible upstream editing stacks. The top-three direction ranking was retained: constrained parametric editing, explicit routing boundaries, and exact-versus-paraphrase training breadth. Full synthetic-document training and causal circuit localization remain unperformed.\n\nPinned real local model: Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct revision `989aa7980e4cf806f80c7fef2b1adb7bc71aa306`. Actual execution:33 false-edit runs,2 true-answer controls,4 unchanged evaluations;79,248 local evaluation responses. Main experiment hardware: RTX A6000, torch2.6+cu124 in isolated .venv. Model files/checkpoints stay under this workspace and are Git-ignored. Original torch2.14 inference failed without a C compiler; the working stack is pinned in uv.lock.\n\nLive-catalog API prompt controls:180 successful calls to `qwen/qwen3.8-flash` through OpenRouter, Alibaba provider;10,595 tokens, provider-reported total cost$0.00167245. Complete prompts/responses, catalog metadata, and costs are in results/. These are prompting controls, not remotely trained weights.\n\nPrimary measured protected changes were6.73% for plain FT,4.05% for FT+KL10,7.13% for paraphrase FT+KL10. All primary false edits succeeded at20 steps. Seed11 cross-format audits still answer4 outside the trained answer-only chat interface. Both planned seed-paired tests have Holm-adjustedp=.50. Exact wrappers have architectural noninterference outside their predicate, not evidence of isolated belief change.\n\nSee [REPORT.md](REPORT.md) for resu